#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Despatch Performance Report  (SAIL - EGOM - Iron Ore)
====================================================

Parses the daily "Despatch Performance" WhatsApp messages (iron ore rake
despatch) from .docx / .txt exports and produces a performance report.

What it reads from each message
-------------------------------
    Total Rakes                     -> day's despatch
    Daily COD Plan // Current Mth Avg : 22.09 // 19.00
                                    -> day's COD plan and running month avg
    Cumulative: 19 Rakes            -> month-to-date as stated in the message
    KBR(4): (Daily COD Plan- 2.84)  -> per-mine rakes AND per-mine COD plan
      (1 L+2 F)BSL / 1FRSP          -> per-mine destination split (mine -> plant)
    Jharkhand / Odisha Group        -> group rakes with Lump/Fines split
    Plant Distribution              -> BSL/DSP/RSP/ISP/BSP/Sales/Pellets
      Pellets : [1FBSL,1FRSP,...]   -> pellet rakes by receiving plant a/c
    Rake Types                      -> BOXN / BOYN / BOBSN / GPWIS etc.
    KTR : BSL (2 Rakes)             -> Kuteshwar
    Remarks ::                      -> reasons for shortfall

Reporting conventions
---------------------
  * Financial year runs 1 April to 31 March and is labelled F.Y.2025-2026.
  * Q1 of F.Y.2025-2026 is April-2025 to June-2025.
  * Weeks run strictly Sunday to Saturday and never cross a month boundary,
    so a month beginning or ending mid-week has a short first/last week.
  * Rakes/day for a month uses the calendar days of that month.

Usage
-----
    python despatch_report.py messages.docx
    python despatch_report.py messages.docx --month 2026-08
    python despatch_report.py messages.docx --fy 2026
    python despatch_report.py messages.docx --excel aug26.xlsx
    python despatch_report.py --selftest        # verify the parser

Dependencies: standard library only. Optional: openpyxl (--excel),
matplotlib (--charts).
"""

